---
export const prerender = true;
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Terms of Service | CrawlPact"
  description="Terms governing use of CrawlPact's website, free audit tool, and subscription plans."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-h1 text-neutral-950">Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-supporting text-neutral-500">
      Draft, pending formal legal review before production launch (see SRS §39).
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">The service</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact audits and monitors the publicly declared AI crawler policy of a website you
      specify. CrawlPact evaluates and reports on declared policy and observed responses; it does
      not prove or guarantee that any crawler will obey that policy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">Acceptable targets</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      You may only submit domains you own, manage, or are otherwise authorised to audit. See
      <a href="/acceptable-use" class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2"
        >acceptable use</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">Subscriptions and billing</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      Paid plans are billed annually through Paddle, acting as merchant of record. Paddle handles
      payment collection, tax calculation, receipts, and cancellation. CrawlPact does not store your
      payment card details.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">No guarantee of outcome</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact does not guarantee that any AI crawler will honour a declared policy, that content
      will or will not appear in an AI system's output, or any specific search or AI visibility
      outcome.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-h2 text-neutral-950">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      These terms may be updated as the product develops; material changes will be reflected on this
      page with an updated date once the product reaches general availability.
    </p>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
